## 3. Production Use in user-sovereign systems

Production Use of an Application Work by any person is permitted only in a Qualifying Sovereign System. There is no
private-user Production Use exception. Packaging by an App Licensor or Authorized Distributor, authorized Conveying,
and Private Assembly that is not Production Use may occur before or without qualification. An Authorized Distributor
need not evaluate a Recipient's present or future system.

A Sovereign User, Authorized Distributor, or separately authorized operator may rely in good faith on the Kernel
Provider's current disclosures unless that person knows they are materially false or caused or controls the defect. Such
a person does not violate this License solely because an unknown provider defect means the system did not qualify. This
protection ends for ordinary Production Use after actual knowledge of a material qualification failure, but continues
for the minimum activity reasonably necessary to inspect, export, recover, migrate, delete, safely uninstall, or wind
down the Application Work and User Data. New or expanded Production Use must wait until the defect is cured.

No Sovereign User must investigate, monitor, prove, audit, or document qualification; publish source; keep a package or
controller history; create a record; register anything; run a source service; or cure an upstream violation. These
protections remove compliance work from the user but do not authorize an App Modification or known nonqualifying
Production Use.

This section does not authorize multi-user hosting, durable third-party tenancy, or knowing coordination with a provider
to evade this License. It does not excuse the Kernel Provider, Application operator, or other person responsible for a
violation. A compliance request concerning a provider-controlled defect must be directed to the responsible provider or
operator, not to a Sovereign User that neither caused nor controls it.

## 4. Inspection, testing, security, and recovery

Outside a Qualifying Sovereign System You may retain and run an Authorized Copy without ordinary operational benefit
only as reasonably necessary to inspect, evaluate, perform compatibility or recovery testing, archive, recover, or
perform Security Research on that unchanged Application Work. You may use Authorized Technical Transformations but may
not make an App Modification. Any resulting Production Use must independently satisfy section 3.

This permission includes automated testing, interoperability testing, incident response, forensics, and recovery
testing of an Authorized Copy. Use synthetic, deidentified, or minimum authorized fixture data and delete it when no
longer needed. It does not grant a general development right or permission to prepare, retain, run, or distribute a
modified build.

This section does not permit ordinary operational benefit, an end-user service, production hosting, durable third-party
tenancy, retention of unrelated personal data, avoidable harm, or disguising production as evaluation, testing,
classroom, archival, or research activity. A right that applicable law makes non-waivable remains unaffected.

## 5. Authorized distribution, packages, source transparency, and network operation

### 5.1 Authorized copies only

This License does not authorize You to Convey or Operate an Application Work for another. An App Licensor may do so as
copyright owner and may separately appoint an Authorized Distributor or operator. That separate authority must identify
the authorized person or distribution mechanism and the versions and conduct it covers; source visibility or possession
alone is not authority.

When an App Licensor or Authorized Distributor Conveys an Application Work, it must preserve accurate copyright,
authorship, patent, license, and warranty notices; supply this License and required third-party notices; and prominently
disclose the Production Use condition. It must not present an App Modification as an Authorized Copy unless every
relevant App Licensor separately approved that version.

### 5.2 Complete App Source

When an App Licensor or Authorized Distributor Conveys App Source, it must include Complete App Source or a functioning
no-charge link to it. When it Conveys Executable Form, it must supply a retainable copy of Complete App Source with it or
provide no-charge network access to copy it. Including a retainable source copy fully satisfies this section for that
copy and creates no continuing hosting duty. If it uses only a link, the person that controls the offer must keep it
available while Conveying that version and for three years after the last Conveyance. No public repository, account,
registration, or disclosure to anyone other than a Recipient is required. Source access must require no broader
identification, contract, or payment than executable access.

Complete App Source is supplied for inspection, security review, and verification. Its availability does not grant
permission to modify, build a changed version, create a derivative work, or redistribute source or executable copies.
A neutral storage, network, or delivery provider acting solely at an App Licensor's or Authorized Distributor's
direction does not receive broader rights and may retain copies only as needed for that authorized service.

### 5.3 Application package information and private assembly

When an App Licensor or Authorized Distributor Conveys an Application Package, it must include or identify the
Application and version, this License, required notices, Complete App Source, ordinary dependency manifests or locks,
declared Capabilities, and released schemas and migrations. An ordinary manifest and source tree may satisfy this
section, and a packaging tool may generate or supplement the information. It need supply only accurate materials and
facts under its control.

No App Licensor, App Contributor, Application author, Authorized Distributor, authorized operator, or Sovereign User
must predict, calculate, approve, publish, register, or retain a future package combination, compiler output,
installation payload, combined Wasm, installed-module hash, Kernel-terms selection, actor evidence, or deployment
history. No installed-system legal record, public registry, content-addressed store, or on-canister compliance record is
required. Private Assembly creates none of these duties.

A Kernel may create optional local integrity, compatibility, migration, or recovery information for product safety. Such
information is not a condition of permission or qualification.

### 5.4 Network operation

When an App Licensor or separately authorized operator Operates an Application Work for a Recipient, that Recipient must
have a prominent, convenient, no-charge way to obtain the exact Complete App Source, this License, and third-party
notices throughout operation. An unmodified Kernel feature satisfies this condition if the authorized operator supplies
the exact materials and does not suppress the feature. It need not identify or contact Recipients individually, keep a
Recipient list, use a public repository, or continue hosting after operation ends. Section 5.2 separately governs an
Authorized Copy that is Conveyed.

Source for installed or running code may not be embargoed. Exploit instructions, vulnerability analysis, private
credentials, and unrelated security material are not Complete App Source and may be handled through coordinated
disclosure.

## 6. Assembly with Kernels and independent dependencies

You may inspect, validate, store, install, and perform Authorized Technical Transformations of an Authorized Copy with a
Kernel, Independent Dependencies, and other Applications before deployment and in a Qualifying Sovereign System. This
permission covers only the unchanged Application functionality and does not authorize component extraction or reuse.

The Application Work remains under this License. An independent Kernel, Application, dependency, documented interface,
or neutral generated adapter does not become subject to this License solely because of assembly. This License grants no
rights under another component's license.

An Authorized Technical Transformation does not grant permission for an App Modification, code or assets extracted from
the Application Work, a changed or separately usable derivative, or a nominally separate component used to evade this
License.

A Combined Form Conveyed by an App Licensor or Authorized Distributor must preserve the available legal identities,
notices, and licenses of its components and supply Complete App Source for the Application Work and source required by
each other component's license. Byte-level separation, prevention of compiler inlining, a reproducible executable
mapping, build or deployment records, and digests are not required. Private Assembly is not Conveying a Combined Form.

The Production Use condition restricts only the Application Work, never rights in an independent Kernel. The assembly
exception does not cure incompatibility with GPL, AGPL, or another license.

## 7. Recipients, transfer, and prohibited additional restrictions

Each lawful Recipient of an Authorized Copy automatically receives the section 2 grants directly from every App
Licensor. Sublicensing is not granted or needed. Receipt from an unauthorized source does not itself authorize the copy;
a good-faith recipient may retain it only for the reasonable time needed to obtain an Authorized Copy or safely export,
recover, migrate, or delete User Data.

You may not transfer, forward, mirror, publish, sell, rent, lease, lend, sublicense, or otherwise Convey an Application
Work unless an App Licensor separately makes You an Authorized Distributor. Applicable exhaustion, backup, transfer,
interoperability, observation, study, testing, and similar rights that cannot lawfully be waived remain unaffected.

An Authorized Distributor or separately authorized operator must not impose a license term, royalty for exercising
granted rights, technical restriction, withheld authorization, or other measure that further limits a Recipient's
section 2 rights. The Qualifying Sovereign System condition and reserved rights are part of this License and cannot be
removed by a distributor or operator.

You may not invoke anti-circumvention law or a technological-protection claim to prevent licensed conduct in a
